# UI Safety and Accessibility Standards

These rules are mandatory for all UI code in this clinical decision-support application.

## Destructive Actions

Every server-side destructive action (delete, remove, reset, create-rule, dismiss, reject) MUST use `ConfirmDialog` from `components/ConfirmDialog.tsx`. Never use `window.confirm()` or fire destructive API calls on a bare `onClick`.

```tsx
// BAD — one-click permanent delete
<IconButton onClick={() => deleteCodedLink(id)}><DeleteIcon /></IconButton>

// GOOD — gated by ConfirmDialog
const [confirmDelete, setConfirmDelete] = useState<string | null>(null);
<IconButton onClick={() => setConfirmDelete(id)}><DeleteIcon /></IconButton>
{confirmDelete && (
  <ConfirmDialog
    title="Remove clinical code?"
    body={`This will permanently delete ${term} (${confirmDelete}).`}
    confirmLabel="Remove"
    variant="danger"
    onConfirm={() => { handleRemove(confirmDelete); setConfirmDelete(null); }}
    onCancel={() => setConfirmDelete(null)}
  />
)}
```

## Error Handling

Never swallow API errors. Every fetch must surface failures to the user.

```tsx
// BAD — silent failure looks like empty data
const data = await fetchData().catch(() => []);

// GOOD — per-section error state
try { setData(await fetchData()); }
catch { setSectionError("Unable to load data. Please retry."); }
```

Always check `res.ok` on raw `fetch()` calls before treating as success.

## Keyboard Shortcuts

Keyboard handlers for destructive actions (reject, dismiss, delete) must:
1. Guard against `input`, `textarea`, `contentEditable`, `select`, and `[role="combobox"]`
2. Show a `ConfirmDialog` before executing

```tsx
if (
  e.target instanceof HTMLInputElement ||
  e.target instanceof HTMLTextAreaElement ||
  e.target instanceof HTMLSelectElement ||
  (e.target as HTMLElement).isContentEditable ||
  (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('[role="combobox"]')
) return;
```

## Headings

Every page must have exactly one `<h1>`. Use `component="h1"` on the page title Typography:

```tsx
<Typography variant="h5" component="h1">Settings</Typography>
```

Do not use heading variants on non-heading elements (e.g. sidebar brand).

## Input Labels

All inputs must have programmatic labels. Never rely on `placeholder` alone.

- MUI `TextField`: use the `label` prop, or `aria-label` for search fields.
- `IconButton`: always add `aria-label`.
- `CircularProgress`: always add `aria-label="Loading"`.

## Native Dialogs

Never use `alert()`, `window.confirm()`, or `window.prompt()`. Use MUI `Alert`/`Snackbar` for feedback and `ConfirmDialog` for confirmations.

## Colour Contrast

Text on white must meet WCAG AA (4.5:1 for normal, 3:1 for large text). Banned combinations on white backgrounds: `#94a3b8` (2.4:1), `#e2e8f0` (1.2:1), `rgba(0,0,0,0.38)` (2.7:1). Use theme tokens; minimum caption color is `#6B7280`.

## Empty States

Never `return null` when data is absent. Always render an explanation with navigation:

```tsx
// BAD
if (!data) return null;

// GOOD
if (!data) return (
  <Alert severity="info">No candidate data available. <Link href={backUrl}>Return to encounters</Link></Alert>
);
```
